## Findings

Changes from the Codex draft (~/.bisellium-evidence/W-267-draft/W-267-draft.md), each checked against master 60f6bd5a.

1. Split: process.roles.defined moves to W-267 part 2, after W-274. Today's lex and handoff name eleven ~/.bisellium-evidence scripts and repo scripts that do not exist (review-packet.sh, review-receipt.sh, multilane-spec/{review,resume}.sh, chore-pr.sh), so the rule would block master on day one; W-274 moves them. The draft's "<name> agent" heuristic would also flag "another agent", "Haiku agent" and "an agent" in the current lex. check: none: the rule ships in part 2
2. The per-opus runner lease is cut. SubagentStart carries agent_id and agent_type but no prompt and no tool_use_id, so a pending lease cannot be bound to the right runner when two are dispatched. A missed SubagentStop would lock the opus for the session. One runner per opus becomes Default 4. With no SubagentStart wiring, "print: SubagentStart intentionally absent" stays green. check: packages/shim/test/hooks.test.ts
3. The two settings allow rules are replaced by the hook's own PreToolUse permissionDecision "allow", given only to an authenticated ladder-runner. Claude Code 2.1.280 lists shell allow rules it suspends in auto mode, and a wildcard interpreter or package-manager run rule is the kind it drops. The settings rules would also pre-authorise the main thread. Whether auto mode honours a hook allow is unverified and left to the Patron's live check. check: none: live auto-mode session after merge
4. The draft denied "a ladder command from another subagent", which would refuse the builder's red and the architect's spec verdict (lex §9 steps 1 and 3). There is now an explicit agent_type table. check: packages/cli/src/w267.test.ts
5. Runtime fail-open stated. A hook that is not found, crashes or times out does not block in Claude Code. The command gains "|| exit 2", so not-found and crash block; a timeout still passes and is named as a limit. check: packages/cli/src/w267.test.ts
6. Latency measured: the installed bisellium (tsx loader) takes 1.02-1.13 s per call against the 2 s timeout, on every Bash call by every agent. The bin fast-paths dispatch to a stdlib-only dispatch.ts that Node 25 loads natively (0.16 s measured). check: packages/cli/src/w267.test.ts
7. process.dispatch_guard is static only: CI has no installed bisellium, so a check rule that runs the hook target would fail every CI run. The live probe moves to hooks check --repo. check: process.dispatch_guard
8. The draft said readJsonFromStream is size-bounded and that runHookEvent rejects oversized input. It is time-bounded only (packages/shim/src/hooks/stdin.ts). dispatch.ts caps stdin at 1 MiB itself. check: packages/cli/src/w267.test.ts
9. Every red prints "not ok 1": with --test-name-pattern, node 25.9 numbers only the selected test (verified locally; W-265 b2's red is the precedent). The draft had "not ok 2" to "not ok 6", which would never match. check: brief.admission
